WEBVTT

00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:13,960
I'm curious whether I should be taking iron is the next question.

00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:19,920
So whether a person should be taking iron or not, really depends on their complete

00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:20,920
blood count.

00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:25,920
So their CBC part of their blood test is how you would determine whether a person should

00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:27,840
be taking iron or not.

00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:31,400
So there are several different types of anemia.

00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:39,640
One type of anemia is anemia where you have deficiency, iron deficiency, anemia.

00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:42,200
And those people can be taking iron.

00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:46,480
Now, you have to take other things into consideration as well.

00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:54,800
If on your CBC, you should have also requested on your CBC that you also tested for ferritid.

00:00:54,800 --> 00:01:00,440
Now, ferritid is low, that can be a sign of deficiency as well.

00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:07,720
You would not treat the ferritid low if your red blood cells were within normal limits.

00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:13,720
But if your red blood cells are low, your R-E-W is high and other signs of higher deficiency

00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:14,720
are there.

00:01:14,720 --> 00:01:19,480
But if your ferritid is elevated, then you don't give iron.

00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:24,640
So you have to treat it some other way, but you don't want to give iron if you have elevated

00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:25,640
ferritid.

00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:29,480
You know you have an inflammatory process going on and you have to dig too bad.

00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:34,520
However, just because you have anemia doesn't mean that you should go in even if it's

00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:38,000
iron deficiency anemia, doesn't mean you should go and treat it with iron.

00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,880
Like anything, you need to dig to find out why do I have anemia.

00:01:41,880 --> 00:01:43,600
So are you bleeding?

00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:46,640
Maybe it's just excess blood from you have heavy periods.

00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:49,520
Well, you need to dig to why that is and solve that.

00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:56,160
You don't just treat things with supplements, nor should you just treat things with medication

00:01:56,160 --> 00:02:02,600
without figuring out why in solving that answer to that why first.

00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:07,960
However, if you come to that decision and you're going to use iron, then you have to look

00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:09,360
at all those other factors.

00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:16,080
Also, if you do have cancer, taking iron is an issue, can be an issue too because iron can

00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:17,080
be gobbled up by cancer.

00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:22,320
Because there is another type of anemia called anemia, chronic disease, where stage 4 cancer

00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:27,840
patients will end up showing anemia, and then you want to couple anemia with artimisticid

00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:28,840
as well.

00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:35,760
So if the cancer is going to couple the iron intake with artimisticid as well, because if the

00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:41,720
cancer is going to gobbled up the iron, you may try to, artimisticid is an arm that tends

00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:46,920
to go carried, be carried with iron, and it can be carried into the cancer cell to help

00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:48,240
kill it.

00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:49,240
So that could be beneficial.

